"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1,"offset":2887},"end":{"line":74,"column":45,"offset":2931}}},{"type":"code","lang":"sbpf","meta":null,"value":"call 16   ; Call sol_log_ (helper ID 16)\r\nexit      ; Return using r0 value","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1,"offset":2935},"end":{"line":79,"column":4,"offset":3024}},"data":{"highlightId":"code-4"}},{"type":"mdxJsxFlowElement","name":"ArticleSection","attributes":[{"type":"mdxJsxAttribute","name":"name","value":"Conclusion","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":17,"offset":3044},"end":{"line":81,"column":34,"offset":3061}}},{"type":"mdxJsxAttribute","name":"id","value":"conclusion","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":35,"offset":3062},"end":{"line":81,"column":50,"offset":3077}}},{"type":"mdxJsxAttribute","name":"level","value":"h2","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":51,"offset":3078},"end":{"line":81,"column":61,"offset":3088}}}],"children":[],"position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1,"offset":3028},"end":{"line":81,"column":64,"offset":3091}}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The program:","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1,"offset":3095},"end":{"line":83,"column":13,"offset":3107}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1,"offset":3095},"end":{"line":83,"column":13,"offset":3107}}},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":false,"checked":null,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calls 16 (","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":4,"offset":3112},"end":{"line":84,"column":14,"offset":3122}}},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sol_log_","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":14,"offset":3122},"end":{"line":84,"column":24,"offset":3132}}},{"type":"text","value":") to print the memo to the validator log","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":24,"offset":3132},"end":{"line":84,"column":64,"offset":3172}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":4,"offset":3112},"end":{"line":84,"column":64,"offset":3172}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1,"offset":3109},"end":{"line":84,"column":64,"offset":3172}}},{"type":"listItem","spread":false,"checked":null,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exits using the value in ","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":4,"offset":3177},"end":{"line":85,"column":29,"offset":3202}}},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"r0","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":29,"offset":3202},"end":{"line":85,"column":33,"offset":3206}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":4,"offset":3177},"end":{"line":85,"column":33,"offset":3206}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1,"offset":3174},"end":{"line":85,"column":33,"offset":3206}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1,"offset":3109},"end":{"line":85,"column":33,"offset":3206}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1,"offset":0},"end":{"line":85,"column":33,"offset":3206}}},"raw":"import { ArticleSection } from \"../../../../components/ArticleSection/ArticleSection\";\r\n\r\n![Assembly Memo Challenge](/graphics/challenge-banners/assembly-memo.png)\r\n\r\n# Assembly Memo\r\n\r\nIn this unit we'll use sBPF Assembly to create a logging mechanism for our program.\r\n\r\nThe simplicity of a bite-size memo program is the perfect starting point for your sBPF assembly journey!\r\n\r\nIf you're unfamiliar with assembly programming, follow the [introduction to Assembly course](/en/courses/introduction-to-assembly)\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Program Design\" id=\"program-design\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nOur program will simply put the right memory location into the right register and then perform the `sol_log_` syscall. It will look like this:\r\n\r\n```sbpf\r\n.equ NUM_ACCOUNTS, 0x00\r\n.equ DATA_LEN, 0x08\r\n.equ DATA, 0x10\r\n.globl entrypoint\r\nentrypoint:\r\n  ldxdw r0, [r1+NUM_ACCOUNTS]\r\n  ldxdw r2, [r1+DATA_LEN]\r\n  add64 r1, DATA\r\n  call sol_log_\r\n  exit\r\n```\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Memory Offsets\" id=\"memory-offsets\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nThe program begins by declaring three `.equ` constants that define the memory layout of our instruction data:\r\n\r\n```sbpf\r\n.equ NUM_ACCOUNTS, 0x00  ; Offset for number of accounts\r\n.equ DATA_LEN, 0x08      ; Offset for data length\r\n.equ DATA, 0x10          ; Offset for actual data\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese constants mark the byte-offsets relative to the entry-buffer pointer in `r1`:\r\n- `NUM_ACCOUNTS` (0x0000): Points to the account count in the instruction data header for validation\r\n- `DATA_LEN` (0x08): Points to the instruction data length in the instruction data header\r\n- `DATA` (0x10): Points to the instruction data in the instruction data header\r\n\r\nUnlike high-level languages that abstract memory layout, assembly requires knowing exactly where every piece of data lives.\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Entrypoint and Initial Validation\" id=\"entrypoint-and-validations\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\n```sbpf\r\n.globl entrypoint\r\nentrypoint:\r\n  ldxdw r0, [r1+NUM_ACCOUNTS]   ; Load number of accounts into r0\r\n```\r\n\r\nEvery sBPF program starts at a global `.entrypoint` symbol. The Solana runtime provides account and instruction data through register `r1`.\r\n\r\nThis first instruction then loads the number of accounts into `r0`. Since `r0` is the register the VM reads on exit, this serves two purposes:\r\n1. It loads the account count for our use\r\n2. It ensures the program will fail automatically if any accounts are passed (non-zero value in r0)\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Sol Log Syscall\" id=\"sol-log-syscall\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nNext, we prepare the arguments for the `sol_log_` syscall:\r\n\r\n```sbpf\r\nldxdw r2, [r1+DATA_LEN]   ; Load length of memo into r2\r\nadd64  r1, DATA           ; Adjust r1 to point to memo bytes\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese instructions set up the arguments for `sol_log_`:\r\n- `r2` receives the length of the memo data\r\n- `r1` is adjusted to point directly to the memo bytes\r\n\r\nAnd after that, we call `sol_log_` and exit:\r\n\r\n```sbpf\r\ncall 16   ; Call sol_log_ (helper ID 16)\r\nexit      ; Return using r0 value\r\n```\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Conclusion\" id=\"conclusion\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nThe program:\r\n1. Calls 16 (`sol_log_`) to print the memo to the validator log\r\n2. Exits using the value in `r0`","highlightedCode":{"code-0":{"lang":"sbpf","hast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"pre","properties":{"class":"shiki Kiloshift","style":"background-color:#11141a;color:#f6f6f4","tabindex":"0"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F6F6F4"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":".equ NUM_ACCOUNTS, "}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F1FA8C"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"0x00"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F6F6F4"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":".equ DATA_LEN, "}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F1FA8C"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"0x08"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F6F6F4"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":".equ DATA, "}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F1FA8C"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"0x10"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#FF79C6"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":".globl"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F6F6F4"},"children":[{"type":